  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef has a sequence AAA of 2⋅N2 \\cdot N2⋅N integers containing all natural numbers from 111 to NNN **exactly twice**.\n\nLet a sequence BBB containing KKK elements be a subsequence of AAA. We define a **strictly increasing** index sequence I(B)=[I1,I2,…,IK]I(B) = [I_1, I_2, \\ldots, I_K]I(B)=[I1​,I2​,…,IK​] such that, BBB can be written as [AI1,AI2,…,AIK][A_{I_1}, A_{I_2}, \\ldots, A_{I_K}][AI1​​,AI2​​,…,AIK​​].\n\nA pair of subsequences (P,Q)(P,Q)(P,Q) is said to be good if all of the following conditions satisfy:\n\n\nBoth subsequences have the same length. In other words, ∣P∣=∣Q∣|P| = |Q|∣P∣=∣Q∣, where ∣P∣|P|∣P∣ and ∣Q∣|Q|∣Q∣ denote the lengths of PPP and QQQ respectively;\nThe subsequences PPP and QQQ are disjoint. In other words, there are **no** common elements between I(P)I(P)I(P) and I(Q)I(Q)I(Q);\nThe subsequences are equal. In other words, Pj=QjP_j = Q_jPj​=Qj​ for all (1≤j≤∣P∣)(1\\le j \\le |P|)(1≤j≤∣P∣).\nFind the total number of **distinct ordered** pairs of subsequences (P,Q)(P,Q)(P,Q) that are good.\n\nTwo ordered pairs (P1,Q1)(P_1, Q_1)(P1​,Q1​) and (P2,Q2)(P_2, Q_2)(P2​,Q2​) are considered different iff I(P1)≠I(P2)I(P_1) \\ne I(P_2)I(P1​)=I(P2​) or I(Q1)≠I(Q2)I(Q_1) \\ne I(Q_2)I(Q1​)=I(Q2​).\n\nSince the answer can be very large, print it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line contains TTT − the number of test cases. The description of the test cases is as follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN − the value of NNN.\nThe second line of each test case contains 2⋅N2 \\cdot N2⋅N integers A1,A2,…,A2⋅NA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_{2 \\cdot N}A1​,A2​,…,A2⋅N​​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output a single integer − the total number of **distinct ordered** pairs of subsequences (P,Q)(P,Q)(P,Q) that are good modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤2⋅1051 \\leq T \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤T≤2⋅105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤N1 \\leq A_i \\leq N1≤Ai​≤N",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 6⋅1056\\cdot 10^56⋅105."
    ],
